course: dictionary
lesson: 1443
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The lovely canary-coloured cart lies on its side, smashed beyond repair» shows that a cart is a vehicle, because a vehicle can be smashed and can lie on its side. In a supermarket, the same word would mean something very different.
explain: Phrases can change a word's meaning too. «Put the cart before the horse» is a saying, so do not look for real carts and horses. It means doing things in the wrong order. When you meet a saying, read the whole idea rather than each word on its own.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Real rats eat almost anything and spread round the world on people's ships and carts.» If cart means a vehicle with wheels, the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A cart is a vehicle with two or four wheels, pulled by a horse or other animal, or pushed by hand, used to carry things.
fact: In the USA and Canada, a cart is a shopping trolley in a supermarket.
fact: An online cart is the list of things you plan to buy on a website, and you should never buy from one without an adult.
fact: To cart is to carry something heavy or awkward, often a long way.
fact: «Wheeled carts appeared about 5,500 years ago», so carts are very old, older than many things we use today.
exercise: In «Real rats eat almost anything and spread round the world on people's ships and carts», what is a cart? | *A vehicle with wheels, used to carry things | A kind of ship | A small animal that eats almost anything | A bird in a cage
exercise: What does «put the cart before the horse» mean? | Buy a vehicle | Wash the horse before the cart | *Do things in the wrong order | Go faster than a horse
exercise: In the USA or Canada, what is a cart in a supermarket? | *A shopping trolley | A list of things to buy online | A horse-drawn wagon | A kind of petrol station
test: «To cart is to carry something heavy or awkward.» Which word could replace cart in «The farmer had to ___ the sacks of potatoes all the way to the barn»? | Sang | Dropped | Cooked | *Carted
test: What is an online cart? | *The list of things you plan to buy on a website | A safe place to keep your money | A bicycle for the internet | A game you play with a friend
exam: Which option uses cart to mean a vehicle? | *Farmers used horse-drawn carts to carry crops before lorries | Her online cart had twelve games in it | You must cart the boxes to the car | Put the cart before the horse
